    "html_url": "https://github.com/nelsong6/shows/commit/7c8bf6148824473453e345fc1f278a224a6de10b",
    "message": "desktop: flush SSE status frames so the last change before idle is delivered\n\nThe titlebar never returned after unpinning while the video was paused. The\nroot cause was in the status stream, not the pin logic: tiny_http buffers the\nresponse in a 1024-byte BufWriter and never flushes a streaming body, so a\nsub-1 KiB status frame sits unsent until enough following bytes overflow the\nbuffer. With a paused video no further frames follow, so the unpin's\nwindow_on_top=false never reached the overlay — it stayed \"pinned\" (titlebar\nhidden, video-surface drag armed) even though the host had already unpinned.\nThis is pre-existing and is why the earlier frontend work couldn't cure it.\n\nFix: when the status stream would idle after delivering a frame, emit a \u003e1 KiB\nSSE comment (clients ignore ':'-prefixed lines) so the BufWriter overflows and\npushes that frame to the socket at once. Verified with a live SSE capture: the\nunpin's false now arrives ~150ms after the POST instead of never; unit test\nlocks the idle-flush behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
