        "author_association": "OWNER",
        "body": "## Symptoms (reported by user, reproducible)\n- **Pin → can't move the window**: after clicking pin, the surface-drag is dead — clicking/dragging the video no longer moves the window.\n- **Unpin → no titlebar**: after clicking unpin, the custom titlebar does not reappear (window is \"effectively still pinned\").\n- **Intermittent** — \"at random times\", not every time.\n- **Double-click confusion**: clicking the pin button twice quickly \"doesn't know what to do\".\n\n## Root mechanism (what's established)\nBoth primary symptoms reduce to one thing: **the overlay's host-confirmed `status.window_on_top` is not updating.**\n- The surface-drag gate keys on it (`hostOnTopRef`), so when it's stale-false after a pin, drag is dead.\n- The titlebar render condition keys on it (`!status.window_on_top`), so when it's stale-true after an unpin, the titlebar stays hidden.\n\nSo the question is narrow: **why does the host's `window_on_top` change not reliably reach the overlay?**\n\n## Architecture / why it's fragile (read first)\n- Pin uses optimistic-UI + idempotent `POST /stay-on-top` + reconcile-over-SSE (ADR-0001).\n- **Critical asymmetry:** `window_on_top` is **echoed only on change**, unlike pause/volume which ride every mpv heartbeat. So a single lost/coalesced SSE frame **strands** the state with **no self-heal** — pause/volume recover next heartbeat; pin never does.\n- Contract: `docs/feature-contracts/desktop-shell.md` → \"Pin toggle: one click, one command\". Read it.\n\n## History — this was fixed once, on pure main\nPR #3 (session \"shows: pin\") fixed the identical bug (\"titlebar doesn't show on unpin\") and the user confirmed \"it's working.\" Its cure (assistant's words): the **SSE stream flush** (`flush_comment` in `webserver.rs`, the \u003e1 KiB comment that forces tiny_http's `BufWriter` to flush a sub-1 KiB streaming frame). That fix is present in the current code. **Yet the bug is back** — so #3's fix is either incomplete (handles the consistent case, not the intermittent one) or there is a residual delivery hole.\n\n## Ruled out (do not re-investigate)\n- **NOT the memory-leak / Present-gate change.** A prior change gated the video `Present` behind \"new frame\"; the overlay is coupled to the per-tick present, so that *looked* like the cause. It was **reverted** (only `gl.render` is gated now; `Present`+`Commit` run every tick) and **pin is still broken**. So the present-gate is not it.\n\n## Concrete leads for the next agent\n1. **Instrument the actual SSE delivery.** Log, at the overlay's `EventSource.onmessage`, every received `window_on_top`; and log each host `notify()`/broadcast. The whole question is whether the host's `window_on_top=false` frame *reaches* the overlay. If pause/volume frames arrive but the `window_on_top` change does not, the change-frame is being lost or coalesced specifically (suspect the single-slot `state.next` coalescing in `StatusStream` + the `flush_pending` logic in `webserver.rs:1189-1225`).\n2. **Make `window_on_top` self-healing** (most robust, matches the contract's own diagnosis). Either (a) include the current `window_on_top` in *every* status broadcast/heartbeat so a lost frame self-heals like pause/volume, or (b) have the frontend re-`GET /status` ~800 ms after a `/stay-on-top` POST if the echo hasn't arrived, and apply it.\n3. **400 ms `togglePin` guard** (`App.tsx:~435`) swallows genuine rapid double-clicks (meant only to drop a synthetic duplicate of one click). Separate, smaller bug; shrink the window or dedup differently.\n\n## Key files\n- `desktop-rs/frontend/src/App.tsx` — `onTopSync`, `pumpOnTopQueue`, reconcile effect (~385), `togglePin` (~433), surface-drag gate (~345), titlebar render (~891).\n- `desktop-rs/desktop/src/webserver.rs` — `notify()`/broadcast (~316), `StatusStream` read + `flush_comment` (~1160-1225), `/stay-on-top` (~?), `/pause` (~400).\n- `desktop-rs/desktop/src/compositor.rs` — `WM_SET_STAY_ON_TOP` handler (idempotent set; no-op guard `if is_on_top == desired`), fullscreen/maximize pin coherence, `prepin_rect`.\n\n## Verification bar\nPin/unpin **20+ times each, while paused AND while playing**, including rapid double-clicks. Titlebar must reappear on every unpin; drag must work on every pin. The bug is intermittent — a couple of clean toggles is NOT a pass.",
        "closed_at": "2026-07-10T21:14:56Z",
